spoint PlanetFrame.groundHeightLocal (src/terrain/PlanetFrame.js) folds in the sphere CURVATURE drop so the flat Jolt heightfield matches the CURVED rendered planet surface (radial height h-anchorHeight alone left the collider ABOVE the surface at patch edges -> player-under-terrain, growing as radius shrinks: ~0.5m at 63.6km). Compute the drop R*(1-dot(localToDir,up)) from the tangent offset s=(x^2+z^2)/R^2 as r2/R/((sqrt(1+s)+1)*sqrt(1+s)) - NOT (R+h)*dot-(R+anchorHeight), which subtracts two ~6.36e6 numbers and leaves fp noise ~1e-4 at the anchor instead of exact 0 (broke the anchor==0 unit test). Also tps findSpawnPoints (apps/tps-game/server.js) spawns above max(arena raycast, ctx.terrainHeightAt(x,z)) +3m so players never spawn inside/under the terrain.